  "question": {
    "text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>m ladder leans against a vertical wall. If the top of the ladder begins to slide down the wall at the rate <math><mn>25</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math> , then the rate (in cm/sec.) at which the bottom of the ladder slides away from the wall on the horizontal ground when the top of the ladder is <math><mn>1</mn></math> m above the ground is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>25</mn></math>",
